WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.373
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B one.

2
00:00:05.673 --> 00:00:08.955
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.255 --> 00:00:15.634
Unit eighteen: Linking Words (although/despite). Today you will show contrast with although, despite and however.

4
00:00:15.934 --> 00:00:18.447
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:22.552
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.417 --> 00:00:24.186
Although.

7
00:00:25.183 --> 00:00:28.936
Although means used to show contrast; followed by a clause.

8
00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:31.399
Although it rained, we went out.

9
00:00:31.983 --> 00:00:34.473
Your turn. Say: Although.

10
00:00:37.333 --> 00:00:38.300
Although.

11
00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:39.923
Despite.

12
00:00:40.917 --> 00:00:43.404
Despite means used with a noun or -ing.

13
00:00:44.017 --> 00:00:45.761
Despite the rain, we went.

14
00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:48.909
Your turn. Say: Despite.

15
00:00:51.767 --> 00:00:52.733
Despite.

16
00:00:53.483 --> 00:00:54.635
In spite of.

17
00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:58.311
In spite of means the same meaning as despite.

18
00:00:58.917 --> 00:01:00.974
In spite of the cost, he bought it.

19
00:01:01.583 --> 00:01:03.945
Your turn. Say: In spite of.

20
00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.010
In spite of.

21
00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:09.612
However.

22
00:01:10.617 --> 00:01:13.893
However means used between sentences to show contrast.

23
00:01:14.483 --> 00:01:15.960
However, I was happy.

24
00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:18.715
Your turn. Say: However.

25
00:01:21.567 --> 00:01:22.545
However.

26
00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:24.250
Contrast.

27
00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:27.331
Contrast means a clear difference.

28
00:01:27.917 --> 00:01:29.452
There is a contrast.

29
00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:32.818
Your turn. Say: Contrast.

30
00:01:35.667 --> 00:01:36.912
Contrast.

31
00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:38.732
Concession.

32
00:01:39.717 --> 00:01:42.993
Concession means accepting a point before an opposite one.

33
00:01:43.583 --> 00:01:44.933
It was a concession.

34
00:01:45.517 --> 00:01:48.134
Your turn. Say: Concession.

35
00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:51.955
Concession.

36
00:01:52.717 --> 00:01:53.753
Even though.

37
00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:56.726
Even though means a stronger although.

38
00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:59.293
Even though I was tired, I ran.

39
00:01:59.883 --> 00:02:02.327
Your turn. Say: Even though.

40
00:02:05.167 --> 00:02:06.307
Even though.

41
00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:07.854
But.

42
00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:11.337
But means joins two opposite ideas.

43
00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:13.694
I was tired but happy.

44
00:02:14.283 --> 00:02:16.576
Your turn. Say: But.

45
00:02:19.433 --> 00:02:20.144
But.

46
00:02:20.933 --> 00:02:24.340
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:25.183 --> 00:02:27.682
Visal, say one sentence with although.

48
00:02:28.783 --> 00:02:36.918
Although it was raining, we played football. Although is followed by a clause with a subject and a verb. It shows contrast.

49
00:02:38.017 --> 00:02:39.935
What is the difference with despite?

50
00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:53.109
Despite and in spite of are followed by a noun or an -ing form: Despite the rain, we played. Despite being tired, I studied. Never say despite of.

51
00:02:54.217 --> 00:02:55.671
Where does however go?

52
00:02:56.783 --> 00:03:10.227
However joins two sentences: It was raining. However, we played. Use a full stop or semicolon before it, and a comma after. But joins within a sentence, and even though is a stronger although.

53
00:03:11.367 --> 00:03:13.180
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:14.017 --> 00:03:18.315
Grammar focus: Contrast: although and despite and however.

55
00:03:18.615 --> 00:03:19.744
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:23.042
Although it was raining, we played football.

57
00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:25.996
Despite the rain, we played football.

58
00:03:26.883 --> 00:03:29.663
It was raining. However, we played football.

59
00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:38.421
Although + clause. Despite / in spite of + noun or -ing (never 'despite of'). However starts a new sentence, with a comma after it.

60
00:03:39.183 --> 00:03:43.078
Be careful! Don't say: Despite of the rain, we left.

61
00:03:45.033 --> 00:03:47.323
Say: Despite the rain, we left.

62
00:03:47.623 --> 00:03:49.193
Never use despite of.

63
00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.931
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:54.816
Even So….

65
00:03:55.116 --> 00:03:57.336
Although it was raining, we played football.

66
00:03:58.333 --> 00:04:00.344
Despite the rain, we had a great time.

67
00:04:01.333 --> 00:04:04.041
In spite of being tired, I finished my work.

68
00:04:05.033 --> 00:04:07.871
The road was long. However, we enjoyed the trip.

69
00:04:08.867 --> 00:04:12.329
Even though it was difficult, the contrast made us stronger.

70
00:04:13.433 --> 00:04:17.876
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:18.717 --> 00:04:20.519
blank it was cold, we swam.

72
00:04:20.819 --> 00:04:24.217
A, Despite. B, Although. C, However.

73
00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:29.569
The answer is B: Although.

74
00:04:30.717 --> 00:04:32.368
blank the rain, we went out.

75
00:04:32.668 --> 00:04:36.043
A, Although. B, Despite. C, Even though.

76
00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:41.797
The answer is B: Despite.

77
00:04:42.950 --> 00:04:44.624
Which sentence is correct?

78
00:04:44.924 --> 00:04:50.911
A, Despite of the rain, we left.. B, In spite of the rain, we left.. C, Although the rain, we left..

79
00:04:54.467 --> 00:04:57.267
The answer is B: In spite of the rain, we left..

80
00:04:58.417 --> 00:05:00.788
'However' is usually followed by a blank.

81
00:05:01.088 --> 00:05:04.010
A, comma. B, dash. C, colon.

82
00:05:07.567 --> 00:05:09.137
The answer is A: comma.

83
00:05:10.283 --> 00:05:12.538
According to the reading, how was the road?

84
00:05:12.838 --> 00:05:16.085
A, long. B, short. C, closed.

85
00:05:19.633 --> 00:05:21.563
The answer is A: long.

86
00:05:22.767 --> 00:05:25.837
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:26.683 --> 00:05:30.041
Write a sentence using 'although' and a sentence using 'despite'.

88
00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:40.327
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:40.627 --> 00:05:51.188
Although I was very tired, I finished my homework. Despite the heavy traffic, I arrived on time. I use although with a clause and despite with a noun.

90
00:05:51.488 --> 00:05:53.140
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:54.050 --> 00:05:59.512
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and contrast: although and despite and however.

92
00:05:59.812 --> 00:06:04.299
Today's value is analytical thinking. Look for the pattern underneath the surface.

93
00:06:04.599 --> 00:06:07.065
See you in Unit nineteen. Goodbye!

94
00:06:07.365 --> 00:06:09.960
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

